==German==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gem-pro|ine-pro|inh=1}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|mīden}}, from {{inh|de|goh|mīdan}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*mīþan}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|mijden}} and {{cog|ang|mīþan}} (archaic {{cog|en|mithe}}).

The expected past forms in modern German would be {{m|de||*mitt, *gemitten}} (as still in {{m|de|leiden}}, {{m|de|schneiden}}), but the {{w|Grammatischer Wechsel}} was levelled out (perhaps to avoid the similarity with unrelated {{m|de|mit}}, {{m|de|mitten}}). To {{m|de||meiden}} was then adapted {{m|de|scheiden}}, whose original past participle was {{m|de||gescheiden}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈmaɪ̯dən/|[ˈmaɪ̯.dn̩]|[-dən]}}
* {{audio|de|De-meiden.ogg}}
* {{homophones|de|Maiden}}

